**1. Analysis & Description of the Attached PDF**
The PDF comprises two research papers (2015 JCR and 2017 npj Vaccines) investigating Nano-11, a dendrimer-like α-D-glucan nanoparticle derived from sweet corn, as a vaccine adjuvant. Nano-11, 70-80 nm with a positive surface charge, efficiently delivers protein antigens to dendritic cells (DCs) via phagocytosis. It activates DCs by increasing costimulatory molecule expression (CD80, CD86) and cytokine secretion (IL-1β, IL-12p40). In vivo, Nano-11 significantly boosts antibody responses to antigens like OVA and rPA, comparable to or better than aluminum adjuvants, and targets migratory DCs in draining lymph nodes. It induces a transient, localized inflammatory response that resolves quickly, with no systemic distribution, suggesting a favorable safety profile.

